{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ef48e947a4c70e998653430bb13a9d08a072ac9319e2842cade50995f0f1d32c","digest":{"component_or_area":"repo-isolation test infrastructure","key_entities":["tests/_isolation.py","tests/conftest.py","pytest_sessionfinish","_no_repo_commits","porcelain()","head()","subprocess.run","git status --porcelain","git rev-parse HEAD","GIT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS","_run_process"],"problem_keywords":["subprocess timeout","unbounded git probe","repo isolation","pytest hook","session teardown","process hang"],"propositions":["Git probes in repo-isolation hooks (porcelain and head) executed without subprocess timeout, allowing blocked children to keep pytest alive indefinitely after test completion","The read-only git status and git rev-parse HEAD probes run synchronously in pytest_sessionfinish and the autouse _no_repo_commits fixture with no timeout bound","A fixed 5-second timeout (GIT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS) must be added to both probes and subprocess.TimeoutExpired must be surfaced as an explicit failure rather than collapsed to None","Test monkeypatches of the shared subprocess module could replace the runner before autouse teardown, causing the guard to invoke test doubles; the real runner must be captured at module import as _run_process to isolate the guard from later mocking"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787807263212299001,"uuid":"7a83744c-9aa3-4529-9e7e-0cfcb340dfcb"}